// batch 5 (2026-09-08) -- elongated/gyroelongated bicupolae, cupola-
// rotundas, and birotundas
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * 14 more Johnson solids (J35-J48): the direct sequel to batch 3, using
 * batch 2's prism/antiprism-spacer technique on batch 3's own cupola/
 * rotunda pieces instead of re-deriving anything from scratch.
 *
 * **Construction changed again for this batch, in a way worth recording**:
 * each piece (a single cupola's cap+waist, or a rotunda "half" sliced out
 * of the already-verified J32/J34) was extracted directly from this
 * registry's own verified vertex data -- not re-derived from formulas --
 * then rejoined either directly (reproducing batch 3, as a self-check)
 * or through a prism (elongated, J35-J43) or antiprism (gyroelongated,
 * J44-J48) spacer. Two real bugs were caught by that self-check *before*
 * any new shape was trusted:
 *   1. "gyro" only rotates the CAP by one full waist-ring step
 *      (2*pi/waist_size); the waist ring itself must stay fixed (it's
 *      the shared face) -- an initial attempt rotated cap+waist together
 *      by a HALF step, which moves the ring to new positions instead of
 *      relabeling the same one, silently breaking the shared-face
 *      requirement.
 *   2. a cupola piece and a rotunda piece pulled from *independent*
 *      sources (a standalone cupola plus a rotunda sliced from the
 *      ortho birotunda) are not guaranteed to share a common rotational
 *      registration -- cross-type (cupola+rotunda) pairs had to be
 *      extracted from the SAME already-verified compound (J32/J33)
 *      instead, guaranteeing correct alignment by construction.
 * Both bugs were caught because the self-check (rebuilding J27-J34 from
 * these same extracted primitives) failed loudly with garbage V/E/F and
 * non-uniform edge lengths before either fix -- only trusted for new
 * shapes once it reproduced all 8 batch-3 compounds exactly.
 *
 * Faces come from a real `scipy.spatial.ConvexHull` on each shape's raw
 * vertex set (same method as batch 4), not hand-declared windings.
 * Every one of the 14 was checked for a valid Euler's-formula count,
 * uniform edge length, a sensible face-size mix, AND -- since two of
 * them (J36, J43) are built from an ortho/gyro cupola or rotunda pairing
 * that ISN'T itself a registered Johnson solid (their un-elongated forms
 * coincide with the cuboctahedron, or were the deliberately-excluded
 * "pentagonal gyrobirotunda" from batch 3) -- a rotation-invariant
 * pairwise-distance-histogram cross-check confirming all 14 are mutually
 * distinct AND distinct from every other shape already in this registry.
 * That the elongated/gyroelongated forms of an excluded or coincidental
 * base pairing are still genuinely new, valid, distinct solids is
 * exactly why elongating breaks the batch-3 coincidence in the first
 * place -- adding real height between the two halves means there's no
 * longer any way for the result to degenerate into something else.
 */

