/**
 * 11 more Johnson solids: gyrate (J72), parabigyrate (J73), metabigyrate
 * (J74), trigyrate (J75), diminished (J76), paragyrate diminished
 * (J77), metagyrate diminished (J78), parabidiminished (J80),
 * metabidiminished (J81), gyrate bidiminished (J82), and tridiminished
 * (J83) rhombicosidodecahedron.
 *
 * The rhombicosidodecahedron (RD) decomposes into 12 local "pentagonal
 * cupola" regions -- one per pentagon face, each pentagon surrounded by
 * 5 triangles alternating with 5 squares, exactly matching J5's own
 * band structure, extracted directly from RD's own registered face/
 * edge data (which vertices form each pentagon's "waist" ring), not
 * assumed. Two operations, applied to one or more regions independently
 * (everything else in RD stays completely fixed):
 *   - **gyrate**: rotate one region's pentagon cap by one waist-ring
 *     step (36 degrees) relative to its own decagon waist, using the
 *     same "cap sits at the angular midpoint of alternating base edges"
 *     principle as every cupola construction since batch 1 -- the
 *     gyrated position is simply the OTHER 5 of the waist decagon's 10
 *     edge-midpoints.
 *   - **diminish**: remove one region's 5 pentagon-cap vertices
 *     entirely, exposing its waist decagon as a real face once the
 *     convex hull recomputes without the cap.
 * Which regions can be combined, and what the combination is named,
 * comes from the same face-centroid-angle classification used for the
 * dodecahedron in batch 7 (adjacent/meta/para) -- RD's 12 pentagons
 * correspond directly to the dodecahedron's 12 faces, confirmed to have
 * the identical angle classes (63.4/116.6/180 degrees) before reusing
 * that classification.
 *
 * **Applied batch 8's lesson from the start this time**: every quad
 * face in every candidate was checked by diagonal measurement (a true
 * square has equal diagonals of sqrt(2); a rhombus with the same unit
 * edges does not), not just edge-length uniformity -- all 11 accepted
 * shapes passed with zero non-square quads.
 *
 * **J79 (bigyrate diminished) was attempted and left out.** Gyrating
 * both regions of a para pair (reproducing J73's own already-verified
 * construction) and then diminishing a third region failed with a
 * large, consistent edge-length error -- tried against all 10 possible
 * third-region choices (every region other than the two already
 * gyrated), all failing identically. Since every choice fails the same
 * way, this isn't a matter of picking the wrong region; something about
 * combining two simultaneous gyrations with a further diminish isn't
 * understood well enough yet to construct with confidence, unlike every
 * other combination in this batch, which worked. Left out rather than
 * forced, the same standard as batch 3's excluded gyrobirotunda, batch
 * 7's excluded J64, and batch 8's excluded J66-J71.
 *
 * Faces come from a real `scipy.spatial.ConvexHull`.
 */

